## Structural Map

Key files Claude reads first:
- `lib/main.dart` — entry point, root mount, top-level providers/blocs
- `lib/app.dart` — `MaterialApp.router` / `MaterialApp` configuration
- `lib/features/<feature>/` — feature-first layout (data / domain / presentation)
- `lib/shared/` or `lib/widgets/` — cross-feature widgets, design system primitives
- `lib/services/` — typed API clients (dio/retrofit wrappers)
- `lib/models/` — DTOs, entities, freezed/json_serializable types
- `lib/router/` — go_router or auto_route configuration
- `test/` — unit + widget tests mirroring `lib/` layout
- `integration_test/` — end-to-end flows
- `pubspec.yaml` — package dependencies, asset declarations, flavor configs

Native shells (touched less often, escalate risk when touched):
- `ios/Runner/` — Swift / Obj-C source, Info.plist, entitlements
- `ios/Podfile` + `Podfile.lock` — CocoaPods dependency graph
- `ios/RunnerTests/` — Swift unit tests (XCTest)
- `android/app/src/main/kotlin/` — Kotlin source (Activity, MethodChannel handlers)
- `android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml` — permissions, intents, deep links
- `android/app/build.gradle` + `android/build.gradle` — Gradle config
- `android/app/src/test/` — Kotlin unit tests (JUnit)

Guidance for native edits lives in `flutter-patterns.md §Native Platform Folders`.

Layers and their purpose:
- **Widgets** → presentation; props-only when possible; `const` constructors where allowed
- **Providers / Blocs / Notifiers** → state-management surface (matches the chosen lib)
- **Repositories** → orchestrate data sources; return domain types, not raw HTTP responses
- **Services** → typed wrappers around dio/http; never bare HTTP calls in widgets
- **Models** → immutable data classes (freezed preferred); JSON via json_serializable
- **Tests** → `*_test.dart` colocated under `test/`; widget tests for UI; integration tests for flows

